From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: pm8941-pwrkey: count the key events of a wake

0018 keeps the wake press (and presses in the 3 s after resume) from
userspace, so userspace can no longer see that the power key woke the
system: the pon device's wakeup source never counts anything. The
KONKR Pocket FIT's charge rest needs to tell a power key wake from a
charger (ADSP doorbell, "ipcc-wake") wake.

Count each key event that 0018 drops on the pon device's wakeup source.
---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c
@@ -185,6 +185,8 @@
 		if (pm8941_pwrkey_sleeping)
 			pm8941_pwrkey_ignore_end = ktime_add_ms(ktime_get(),
 						PM8941_PWRKEY_WAKE_IGNORE_MS);
+		/* not reported, but counted: userspace can tell the key woke it */
+		pm_wakeup_dev_event(pwrkey->dev, 0, false);
 		dev_dbg(pwrkey->dev, "ignoring the wake key event (%u)\n", sts);
 		pwrkey->last_status = sts;
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
